 that will experience flash flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of East Central Fremont, Southwestern El Paso\nand Northwestern Pueblo Counties.","ends":"2026-08-26T19:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"El Paso, CO; Fremont, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29fd037288e78d5e86f430e30a1c6c700938d0b4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29fd037288e78d5e86f430e30a1c6c700938d0b4.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 26 at 3:56PM MDT until August 26 at 11:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n629 IN EFFECT UNTIL 11 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING\nAREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 12 COUNTIES\n\nIN CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nFREMONT               TELLER\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nEL PASO\n\nIN SOUTH CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nCOSTILLA\n\nIN SOUTHEAST COLORADO\n\nBENT                  CROWLEY               CUSTER\nHUERFANO              KIOWA                 LAS ANIMAS\nOTERO                 PUEBLO\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF BLANCA, CANON CITY, COLORADO SPRINGS,\nEADS, FORT GARLAND, LA JUNTA, LAS ANIMAS, OLNEY SPRINGS, ORDWAY,\nPENROSE, PETERSON SPACE FORCE BASE, PUEBLO, ROCKY FORD, SAN LUIS,\nSILVER CLIFF, TRINIDAD, WALSENBURG, WESTCLIFFE,\nAND WOODLAND PARK.","ends":"2026-08-26T23:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Bent, CO; Costilla, CO; Crowley, CO; Custer, CO; El Paso, CO; Fremont, CO; Huerfano, CO; Kiowa, CO; Las Animas, CO; Otero, CO; Pueblo, CO; Teller, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c9c54dbd45c61015d10658ba8eddaa9270117297.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c9c54dbd45c61015d10658ba8eddaa9270117297.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 26 at 12:32PM MDT until August 26 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\nwill be possible over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres Burn Scar should prepare for debris flows and stay up to date\nwith information from local authorities. Heavy rainfall could\ntrigger flash flooding of low-lying areas and debris flows in and\nnear recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel and Highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-26T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9ff2c4a7c1a7690fe1b763a7ff251163efdc6a00.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9ff2c4a7c1a7690fe1b763a7ff251163efdc6a00.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 26 at 12:32PM MDT until August 27 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\nwill be possible over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres Burn Scar should prepare for debris flows and stay up to date\nwith information from local authorities. Heavy rainfall could\ntrigger flash flooding of low-lying areas and debris flows in and\nnear recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weath